[{"text": "I now give the floor to her excellency", "start": 2.32, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "Mary Edith Tacila Yanamubi,", "start": 5.12, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "Minister of Foreign Affairs and", "start": 8.639, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "Cooperation in charge of integration", "start": 10.48, "duration": 8.44}, {"text": "and the diaspora of Gaboon.", "start": 14.08, "duration": 4.84}, {"text": "President,", "start": 39.04, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": ">> Mr. President of the General Assembly,", "start": 40.96, "duration": 6.32}, {"text": "Mr. United Nations Secretary General,", "start": 44.079, "duration": 5.281}, {"text": "excellencies, heads of delegation,", "start": 47.28, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "ladies and gentlemen,", "start": 49.36, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "President of the General Assembly, allow", "start": 52.32, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "me to begin by conveying to you the warm", "start": 54.879, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "congratulations of his excellency Mr.", "start": 57.92, "duration": 6.08}, {"text": "Bree Clair Oligma, president of the", "start": 60.64, "duration": 6.24}, {"text": "Gabanese Republic on your outstanding", "start": 64.0, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "election to preside over this 81st", "start": 66.88, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "session of the General Assembly. I wish", "start": 69.2, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "to assure you right now of my", "start": 71.76, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "delegation's full support and express", "start": 74.08, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "the hope that your term of office will", "start": 76.64, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "be marked by a spirit of listening and", "start": 78.96, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "dialogue and by the tireless pursuit of", "start": 81.439, "duration": 3.281}, {"text": "compromise in the service of", "start": 83.36, "duration": 5.399}, {"text": "international peace and cooperation.", "start": 84.72, "duration": 4.039}, {"text": "As", "start": 89.2, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "the secretary general of the UN, Antonio", "start": 90.96, "duration": 4.159}, {"text": "Guter comes to the end of his second", "start": 93.2, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "term. The president of the Gabanese", "start": 95.119, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "Republic pays special tribute to him for", "start": 97.28, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "his steadfast commitment to", "start": 99.6, "duration": 3.36}, {"text": "multilateralism and to upholding the", "start": 100.96, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "principles enshrined in the United", "start": 102.96, "duration": 5.6}, {"text": "Nations Charter. Ladies and gentlemen,", "start": 105.04, "duration": 6.079}, {"text": "Gabon fully aligns itself with the theme", "start": 108.56, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "for this session, restoring trust,", "start": 111.119, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "managing transformation,", "start": 113.68, "duration": 6.719}, {"text": "a united nations that delivers for all.", "start": 115.759, "duration": 7.281}, {"text": "This theme comes at a pivotal time in", "start": 120.399, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "international history. Our world is", "start": 123.04, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "beset by numerous profound and", "start": 125.92, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "interconnected crises.", "start": 128.8, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "Armed conflicts are becoming more", "start": 131.039, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "protracted. Geopolitical tensions are", "start": 133.76, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "intensifying. Inequalities persist.", "start": 136.319, "duration": 5.841}, {"text": "Climate change is accelerating. And", "start": 139.52, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "humanitarian emergencies are", "start": 142.16, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "multiplying.", "start": 144.4, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "These challenges are compounded by the", "start": 146.239, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "economic and social consequences of", "start": 148.879, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "successive crisis, food insecurity, the", "start": 150.879, "duration": 5.761}, {"text": "forced displacement of populations, the", "start": 154.0, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "risks associated with cyber crime, and", "start": 156.64, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "the upheavalss brought about by emerging", "start": 158.56, "duration": 3.759}, {"text": "technologies.", "start": 160.48, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "These realities are are severely testing", "start": 162.319, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "the international community's ability to", "start": 165.44, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "act together.", "start": 167.92, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "In this uncertain environment, there is", "start": 169.84, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "one value that can still guide us. Trust", "start": 172.64, "duration": 6.879}, {"text": "for Gabon. Restoring trust among nations", "start": 176.64, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "requires more than ever a return to the", "start": 179.519, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "fundamental principles of international", "start": 181.68, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "law in general and of the charter of the", "start": 183.599, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "United Nations in particular. In this", "start": 186.08, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "spirit, my country reaffirms its", "start": 188.72, "duration": 3.2}, {"text": "commitment to the principle of", "start": 190.64, "duration": 3.599}, {"text": "non-inference in the domestic affairs of", "start": 191.92, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "states and to the respect for their", "start": 194.239, "duration": 7.08}, {"text": "sovereignty and territorial integrity.", "start": 196.879, "duration": 4.44}, {"text": "Against this backdrop, Gabon once again", "start": 202.159, "duration": 6.16}, {"text": "welcomes the adoption of resolution 2797", "start": 204.64, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "of 2025,", "start": 208.319, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "which has injected fresh impetus into", "start": 210.08, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "the settlement of the regional dispute", "start": 212.319, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "over the Moroccan Sahara based", "start": 214.159, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "exclusively on the autonomy plan under", "start": 216.48, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Moroccan sovereignty.", "start": 218.959, "duration": 4.721}, {"text": "Mr. President, restoring trust depends", "start": 221.12, "duration": 5.199}, {"text": "above all on concrete action that", "start": 223.68, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "enables us to address", "start": 226.319, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "together global challenges relating to", "start": 228.959, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "peace and security, climate change,", "start": 231.12, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "sustainable development and pandemics.", "start": 233.28, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "Accordingly, in the face of human", "start": 236.239, "duration": 3.681}, {"text": "tragedies across the world and", "start": 238.239, "duration": 3.601}, {"text": "particularly in Africa, greater", "start": 239.92, "duration": 4.959}, {"text": "collective engagement is essential.", "start": 241.84, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "This need for inclusiveness is", "start": 244.879, "duration": 3.841}, {"text": "particularly important in the Gulf of", "start": 246.959, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Guinea, a maritime area whose importance", "start": 248.72, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "to international trade is growing by the", "start": 251.519, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "day.", "start": 254.0, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Consequently, Gabon calls for a", "start": 255.84, "duration": 5.119}, {"text": "substantial strengthening of security in", "start": 258.56, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "this strategic area which represents a", "start": 260.959, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "foundation for shared prosperity.", "start": 263.84, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "Mr. President Gabong in its capacity as", "start": 266.479, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "member of the African Union's Peace and", "start": 269.36, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "Security Council stresses the urgent", "start": 271.6, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "need to implement UN Security Council", "start": 273.84, "duration": 5.76}, {"text": "resolution 2719 on the financing of", "start": 277.12, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "peacekeeping operations on the", "start": 279.6, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "continent. Fulfilling this commitment", "start": 280.8, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "would help consolidate peace in Africa", "start": 283.68, "duration": 4.239}, {"text": "and strengthen cooperation between the", "start": 285.6, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "UN Security Council and the AU's Peace", "start": 287.919, "duration": 5.601}, {"text": "and Security Council.", "start": 290.96, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "Trust also depends on honoring", "start": 293.52, "duration": 5.92}, {"text": "commitments made at the regional level.", "start": 296.16, "duration": 6.72}, {"text": "Under the leadership of his excellency", "start": 299.44, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "Bree", "start": 302.88, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "Oligi, President of the Republic, head", "start": 304.56, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "of state and head of government, Gabon", "start": 307.12, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "has made dialogue, peace, and respect", "start": 309.68, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "for its international commitments the", "start": 311.52, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "guiding principles of its diplomatic", "start": 313.36, "duration": 5.36}, {"text": "action. Ladies and gentlemen, managing", "start": 315.52, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "transformation as the theme of our", "start": 318.72, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "session calls on us to do also means", "start": 320.72, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "knowing how to guide change at the", "start": 323.199, "duration": 3.521}, {"text": "national level. In this regard, under", "start": 324.72, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "the leadership of the president of the", "start": 326.72, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "republic, Gabon is continuing its", "start": 328.88, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "social, environmental and economic", "start": 331.28, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "transformation as set out in our", "start": 333.44, "duration": 4.479}, {"text": "national growth and development plan,", "start": 335.6, "duration": 6.8}, {"text": "the PNC for 2026 2030.", "start": 337.919, "duration": 6.56}, {"text": "This development plan also stresses", "start": 342.4, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "improving the living conditions of our", "start": 344.479, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "people, particularly through new", "start": 346.24, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "administrative hospital and educational", "start": 348.639, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "infrastructure in keeping with the", "start": 350.88, "duration": 4.96}, {"text": "sustainable development goals.", "start": 352.639, "duration": 5.84}, {"text": "In light of all of the above, my country", "start": 355.84, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "calls for a renewed partnership based on", "start": 358.479, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "mutual respect, shared responsibility,", "start": 361.12, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "and concrete commitments.", "start": 363.759, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "Such a partnership must promote the", "start": 366.4, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "local processing of our natural", "start": 369.28, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "resources, the diversification of our", "start": 371.28, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "economy, technology transfer, and the", "start": 373.28, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "strengthening of national capacities.", "start": 375.52, "duration": 7.519}, {"text": "President, restoring trust also involves", "start": 378.72, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "reforming the international financial", "start": 383.039, "duration": 3.6}, {"text": "architecture,", "start": 385.039, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "making it more equitable, inclusive, and", "start": 386.639, "duration": 7.201}, {"text": "better tailored to today's challenges.", "start": 389.84, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "Without this reform, it is becoming", "start": 393.84, "duration": 4.4}, {"text": "almost impossible to mobilize", "start": 396.24, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "development funding, particularly green", "start": 398.24, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "finance.", "start": 400.72, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "Gabon, a country with extensive forest", "start": 403.28, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "cover and a low deforestation rate, as", "start": 405.759, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "well as a major car being a major carbon", "start": 408.639, "duration": 3.921}, {"text": "sink, therefore calls for greater", "start": 410.8, "duration": 3.44}, {"text": "recognition of its contribution to", "start": 412.56, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "global climate regulation and the", "start": 414.24, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "ecosystem services that it provides to", "start": 416.639, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "humanity. These must be properly valued", "start": 418.639, "duration": 7.68}, {"text": "and give rise to fair, adequate,", "start": 422.56, "duration": 6.479}, {"text": "predictable and sustainable financing.", "start": 426.319, "duration": 5.041}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 429.039, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "while it's true that digital", "start": 431.36, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "transformation offers considerable", "start": 433.039, "duration": 5.361}, {"text": "opportunities, it also entails risk,", "start": 435.36, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "infringements of privacy,", "start": 438.4, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "disinformation, cyber crime, and the", "start": 440.4, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "irresponsible use of emerging", "start": 443.199, "duration": 3.681}, {"text": "technologies.", "start": 444.88, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "The absence of an effective", "start": 446.88, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "international legal framework", "start": 448.88, "duration": 5.039}, {"text": "leaves the way open for all of these", "start": 451.36, "duration": 5.279}, {"text": "abuses to arise, posing a direct threat", "start": 453.919, "duration": 4.481}, {"text": "to the security of our states and the", "start": 456.639, "duration": 4.161}, {"text": "fundamental rights of our citizens.", "start": 458.4, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "Having already suffered from these", "start": 460.8, "duration": 4.799}, {"text": "various pericious effects, Gabon has had", "start": 462.88, "duration": 5.759}, {"text": "to introduce more appropriate and secure", "start": 465.599, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "regulation of the digital and artificial", "start": 468.639, "duration": 5.921}, {"text": "intelligence sectors through temporary", "start": 470.479, "duration": 6.0}, {"text": "and proportionate measures motivated", "start": 474.56, "duration": 4.079}, {"text": "solely by the imperative of protecting", "start": 476.479, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "our citizens. Our aim remains to build", "start": 478.639, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "an open and secure digital ecosystem", "start": 481.919, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "that respects freedoms and is fully", "start": 485.039, "duration": 4.081}, {"text": "consistent with our international", "start": 487.599, "duration": 4.16}, {"text": "commitments.", "start": 489.12, "duration": 2.639}, {"text": "Mr. President, if the United Nations is", "start": 492.08, "duration": 6.239}, {"text": "to deliver results for all, it cannot", "start": 495.199, "duration": 6.081}, {"text": "ignore historical debts. Gabon therefore", "start": 498.319, "duration": 5.521}, {"text": "welcomes the adoption of UN General", "start": 501.28, "duration": 5.359}, {"text": "Assembly Resolution 80/250 on the", "start": 503.84, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "African slave trade, characterizing it", "start": 506.639, "duration": 5.441}, {"text": "as the gravest crime against humanity.", "start": 509.28, "duration": 4.72}, {"text": "An organization that delivers results", "start": 512.08, "duration": 4.24}, {"text": "must also be able to reform itself from", "start": 514.0, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "within. The UN must therefore", "start": 516.32, "duration": 4.48}, {"text": "demonstrate its ability to adapt to the", "start": 518.8, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "international context and effectively", "start": 520.8, "duration": 7.56}, {"text": "address the challenges facing the world.", "start": 523.68, "duration": 4.68}, {"text": "This commitment to institutional", "start": 528.48, "duration": 3.68}, {"text": "transformation must take into account", "start": 530.24, "duration": 3.76}, {"text": "the urgent need to reform the security", "start": 532.16, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "council.", "start": 534.0, "duration": 4.399}, {"text": "Indeed, Africa must take its rightful", "start": 536.0, "duration": 5.519}, {"text": "place within the very restricted circle", "start": 538.399, "duration": 6.841}, {"text": "of permanent members.", "start": 541.519, "duration": 3.721}, {"text": "For Gabon, there can be no legitimate", "start": 545.36, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "global governance without equitable", "start": 547.519, "duration": 4.88}, {"text": "African participation in decisions", "start": 549.92, "duration": 4.8}, {"text": "concerning international peace and", "start": 552.399, "duration": 4.321}, {"text": "security.", "start": 554.72, "duration": 3.84}, {"text": "Mr. President,", "start": 556.72, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "Gabon's vision is one of inclusive and", "start": 558.56, "duration": 5.04}, {"text": "reformed multilateralism that takes into", "start": 561.36, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "account the aspirations of peoples,", "start": 563.6, "duration": 5.12}, {"text": "particularly women and young people. It", "start": 566.0, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "is within this framework that the", "start": 568.72, "duration": 4.0}, {"text": "fundamental right of every state to", "start": 570.56, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "chart its own course must be guaranteed.", "start": 572.72, "duration": 7.04}, {"text": "And pursuant to this principle, Gabon", "start": 576.24, "duration": 5.52}, {"text": "here wishes to reaffirm its support for", "start": 579.76, "duration": 5.28}, {"text": "Cuba. Gabon joins the repeated calls by", "start": 581.76, "duration": 5.68}, {"text": "numerous states for the lifting of the", "start": 585.04, "duration": 4.64}, {"text": "embargo.", "start": 587.44, "duration": 4.56}, {"text": "Mr. President, I wish to conclude by", "start": 589.68, "duration": 4.08}, {"text": "saying that Gabon, faithful to its", "start": 592.0, "duration": 4.32}, {"text": "regional and international commitments", "start": 593.76, "duration": 5.44}, {"text": "and confident in a more peaceful future", "start": 596.32, "duration": 6.48}, {"text": "for all, founded on trust, intends to", "start": 599.2, "duration": 6.319}, {"text": "contribute to building a new global", "start": 602.8, "duration": 5.2}, {"text": "order that is more peaceful, more just,", "start": 605.519, "duration": 5.121}, {"text": "more equitable, and more united. Thank", "start": 608.0, "duration": 5.64}, {"text": "you.", "start": 610.64, "duration": 3.0}, {"text": "I thank the Minister of Foreign Affairs", "start": 613.839, "duration": 4.801}, {"text": "and Cooperation in charge of integration", "start": 616.24, "duration": 7.0}, {"text": "and the diaspora of Gabon.", "start": 618.64, "duration": 4.6}, {"text": "I now give the floor to her excellency", "start": 627.04, "duration": 6.4}, {"text": "Anita Anon, Minister", "start": 629.44, "duration": 4.0}]